  "title": "Intracranial EEG from 9 adults during a memory-guided actions experiment (preprocessed epochs, Moraresku et al.)",
  "description": "Preprocessed stereo-EEG epochs from nine patients with drug-resistant epilepsy performing a delayed memory-guided action task at the Motol Epilepsy Center in Prague. The derivative dataset contains bipolar-referenced, notch-filtered and downsampled epochs time-locked to encoding onset, with trial information, channel rejection labels and MNI electrode coordinates. It supports investigation of interactions between dorsal and ventral visual streams and the hippocampus during working memory and action.",
  "methods_description": "Stereo-EEG was recorded with semi-rigid depth electrodes (DIXI Medical) using Quantum NeuroWorks amplifiers at 2048 Hz. The data were downsampled to 512 Hz, notch filtered at 50 Hz and harmonics, and bipolar referenced, with faulty and seizure-onset contacts removed. Data were epoched from -2 to 7.898 s around encoding onset. Patients performed a delayed memory-guided reaching task with a joystick, presented via PsychoPy. Contact positions were localized from CT co-registered to MRI and normalized to MNI space with SPM12.",
